
БЭСМ-6 UNIX Version 7

/tmp is not saved and is cleared at boot. cc(1): char 8 bits,
6 per word; int and long 48. A char * is a word address plus
a byte offset. Core is 32K words.

cc(1) drives cpp(1), as(1) and ld(1), all three on the machine
itself -- it preprocesses, assembles and links its own programs.
It does not compile C yet. disasm(1) reads the a.out back.

Console in UTF-8 prints Cyrillic correctly. File names are
18 Latin characters. The editor is novi(1), full screen; ed(1)
is here too.
